# Build outputs - the crew package ships a compiled exe, but it is assembled
# by the master at generate time, not committed here.
collector.exe
collector-master.exe

# Captures are session data. The rev 5 addendum is explicit that no captures\
# content may ever leave this machine in a crew package; keeping them out of
# git is the same rule applied to the repo.
captures/

# --auto runtime artifacts. Both are written NEXT TO THE EXE at run time and
# belong to whoever is running it, not to the repo:
#   collector-auto.log      what the unattended loop did, for hours at a time
#   collector-settings.txt  the user's own interval/poll choices, generated on
#                           first run. Committing it would push one machine's
#                           settings onto everyone else's.
collector-auto.log
collector-settings.txt
